{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-050", "score": 0.133, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-050 | Study family SF-APPA-050: Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star\n- observed_research_question: Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: A specific opponent play type on the preceding possession suppresses each star's next-possession PPP relative to that star's baseline.\n- observed_result: PUTBACK is top suppressor for 6+ stars (e.g. D. Mitchell 1.178 to 0.884, d=-0.294, n_after=95; B. Beal d=-0.345 n=32; C. Holmgren d=-0.222 n=52). Other tops: TRANSITION (A. Davis -0.058), POST_UP (N. Jokic -0.075), PULL_ [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: No multiplicity correction; n_after is 32-95 for several PUTBACK cells vs thousands of baseline possessions.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 30 stars; min n_after=30\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-079", "score": 0.102, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-079 | Study family SF-APPS-079: State-attribution AUC decomposition of lag-1 memory\n- observed_research_question: State-attribution AUC decomposition of lag-1 memory\n- auto_outcome_status: rejected\n- observed_hypothesis: Lag-1 predictive signal is process/state (pace, play type, transition) rather than outcome persistence.\n- observed_result: Total attributable +0.0614 AUC. outcome_persistence marginal +0.0527 (39% share) unique +0.0069; momentum +0.0494 unique 0; transition_state unique +0.0117 (53% of unique); playtype_state unique +0.0003; lineup_state uni [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Dominant block is outcome persistence/momentum, not play-type or lineup state. Unique signal is mostly transition_state.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 2025-26 test set; original N0->N1 jump +0.0242 for reference\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-059"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-067", "score": 0.1, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-067 | Study family SF-APPS-067: Opponent action T -> your offense T+1 (def-matched 8x8)\n- observed_research_question: Opponent action T -> your offense T+1 (def-matched 8x8)\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: The opponent's previous play type changes your next-possession PPP after matching on defensive team.\n- observed_result: 3/64 FINDING cells survive both matchings: SPOT_UP->TRANSITION ATT=-0.085; POST_UP->TRANSITION -0.083; PNR->DRIVE -0.058 (all also survive +prev_made). PULL_UP->DRIVE dropped as defense-quality confound.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Three cells replicate under def-match, off-match, and prev_made control. Most of 64 are null.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 64 cells tested; 3 FINDING\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPS-067: 'matching primary; sensitivity match on own offense. bh-fdr+placebo+ft-clean. prev_made control. 3/64 finding cells survive bot'\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-060"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-030", "score": 0.097, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-030 | Study family SF-APPS-030: Coaching alignment: BEST/AVOID run rates vs series wins (55 series)\n- observed_research_question: Coaching alignment: BEST/AVOID run rates vs series wins (55 series)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Teams that run BEST counters more (and AVOID less) after suppression win more series.\n- observed_result: % ran BEST 44.7% of triggers / 9.7% volume; % ran AVOID 61.1% / 23.3% volume. Spearman BEST vs won rho=+0.131 p=0.1723; AVOID vs won rho=-0.098 p=0.3099. Mean PPP BEST 1.395 vs AVOID 0.865.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- observed_failure_evidence: Alignment-win Spearmans ns (p=0.172 / 0.310) at n=110 directions; INSUFF_EVIDENCE is 91.5% of triggers.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=110 series-directions\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF05\n- observed_verdict: null\n- observed_failure_type: A_unanswerable"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
